7324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517349 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517377 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517324 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517324 1077 "selection" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517324 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517346 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517324 1079 #uuid "13f111bb-5884-576a-a701-a9d50261c695" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517325 1080 "$228$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517325 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517325 1083 #uuid "1b221c18-6d59-5ed7-9a36-5ef2cdd6198b" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517326 1080 "$-228$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517326 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517326 1083 #uuid "1ea5bf78-0a77-58d1-9e2a-bacef9819834" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517327 1080 "$255$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517327 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517327 1083 #uuid "26ada36c-1091-5f42-8c63-eccc8b641f55" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517328 1080 "$-121$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517328 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517328 1083 #uuid "2b6c992b-a9bf-50ec-a63b-953cb1055324" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517329 1080 "$216$ liters per minute" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517329 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517329 1083 #uuid "2dbec869-25ce-5f09-bec0-1aa8f0c5fc8d" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517330 1080 "$-8$ crocodiles per year" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517330 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517330 1083 #uuid "2e530fff-ce9c-5970-b878-96dbbaeec603" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517331 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517370 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517331 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517331 1071 "The rate $F$ at which a swimming pool is being filled can be modeled as $F(t) = 4t^{2} - 3t$ liters per minute, where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled. The rate at which water is leaking from the pool can be modeled as $L(t) = \\frac{1}{4}t^{2}$ liters per minute, where $t$ is also the time, in minutes, since the pool began to be filled.\n\nWhat is the rate of change of the volume of water in the pool $8$ minutes after the pool began to be filled?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517331 1072 #uuid "4064584b-a92b-5c2b-aee4-39b559d5a1a6" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517331 1074 "The rate of change of the volume of water is the filling rate minus the leaking rate.\n\n$$\nF(t)-L(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=8$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(8)-L(8) & =4(8)^{2}-3(8)-\\frac{1}{4}(8)^{2} \\\\  & =232-16 \\\\  & =216.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $216$ liters per minute." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517332 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517324 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517332 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517332 1071 "The birth rate of crocodiles in a river is modeled by $B(t) = 4 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, while the rate of death is modeled by $D(t) = 1 \\cdot e^{0.25t}$ crocodiles per year, where $t$ represents the number of years since the year $2000$.\n\nWhat was the rate of change of the crocodile population in $2004$? Round your answer to the nearest integer.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517332 1072 #uuid "43cee7e4-6ff9-5eeb-9102-bb7cf335c204" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517332 1074 "The rate of change of the crocodile population is the birth rate minus the death rate.\n\n$$\nB(t)-D(t).\n$$\n\nSince $2004$ is $4$ years after $2000$, substitute $t=4$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(4)-D(4) & =4\\cdot e^{0.25(4)}-1\\cdot e^{0.25(4)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot e^{1} \\\\  & \\approx 8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $8$ crocodiles per year." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517333 1080 "$-35$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517333 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517333 1083 #uuid "48c1409d-fc69-54ea-b9a0-2713986d307a" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517334 1080 "$248$ liters per minute" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517334 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517334 1083 #uuid "51c48530-c821-53d2-8682-e23e9308cc96" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517335 1080 "$\\frac{2}{25}$ percent per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517335 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517335 1083 #uuid "5352939e-cae2-5159-bff4-104d22d61c5b" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517336 1080 "$288$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517336 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517336 1083 #uuid "5baff62d-cf1c-57ec-b9d7-d7a353611316" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517337 1080 "$121$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517337 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517337 1083 #uuid "5bb55a74-3f47-50c3-a675-afc6dec9b4f7" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517322 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517341 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517356 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517373 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517374 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1077 "selection" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517356 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517338 1079 #uuid "5c87e9ae-3f6c-51f1-aa5d-040dc2bf3415" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517327 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517358 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517359 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517363 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517367 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1077 "selection" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517367 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517339 1079 #uuid "60454d3c-fec5-59e1-9526-d25e77d4da41" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517340 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517353 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517340 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517340 1071 "The supplied rate function is $h'(x)=\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{x}}$ thousand dollars per week, for $x>0$.\n\nWhat was the exact rate of change of the stock's value at week $144?$\n\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ thousand dollars per week." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517340 1072 #uuid "631f3d25-1539-5b45-a5e3-359eb72f3729" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517340 1074 "The function ${h}^{'}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the stock, applicable in the domain of $h(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the stock at $x=144$ weeks is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{'}(144) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{144}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{60}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the stock price was $\\frac{1}{60}$ thousand dollars per week." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517341 1080 "$129$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517341 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517341 1083 #uuid "6de37857-a139-5858-9e56-fc09b996a51d" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517342 1080 "1/60" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517342 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517342 1083 #uuid "78aef08d-3e98-50f3-b784-97841b4c299f" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517343 1080 "$1000$ percent per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517343 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517343 1083 #uuid "78f292e0-a2c7-5fcd-8ee3-576f77b454aa" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517344 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517339 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517344 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517344 1071 "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=140t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=90+15\\sin(2\\pi t/14)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $18\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517344 1072 #uuid "7f4724c3-2921-55f4-a281-340d20927d04" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517344 1074 "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(1110-480)/60=10.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(10.5)-C(10.5) & =140(10.5){e}^{-0.2(10.5)}-(90+15\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{14}(10.5))) \\\\  & =140(10.5){e}^{-2.1}-90-15\\sin(\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =140(10.5){e}^{-2.1}-75 \\\\  & \\approx 105.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $105$ cars per hour." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517345 1080 "$-100$ cars per hour" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517345 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517345 1083 #uuid "87ffd388-fbdd-5be1-b220-e00d63314682" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517346 1080 "$8$ crocodiles per year" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517346 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517346 1083 #uuid "89248699-5551-52fc-9603-22d4e2f2008e" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517347 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517364 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517347 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517347 1071 "A factory begins work at $8\\text{:}00$ am. Its order rate is $O(t)=190t e^{-0.2t}$ cars per hour and its completion rate is $C(t)=50+10\\sin(2\\pi t/10)$ cars per hour, where $t$ is hours after work begins. What is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction at the 24-hour time $10\\text{:}30$? Orders enter construction immediately. Round your answer to the nearest integer." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517347 1072 #uuid "8e5ec36a-ecef-5d7c-8e17-1882b5fa8983" 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517347 1074 "The rate of change is the order rate minus the completion rate. The elapsed time is $t=(630-480)/60=2.5$ hours.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(2.5)-C(2.5) & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.2(2.5)}-(50+10\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi }{10}(2.5))) \\\\  & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.5}-50-10\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{2}) \\\\  & =190(2.5){e}^{-0.5}-60 \\\\  & \\approx 228.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change is $228$ cars per hour." 13194139535565 17592186045443 true] [17592186517348 1080 